B. Inspect. Examine repository tree, relevant source files, package manifests, lockfiles, scripts, tests, docs, environment examples, Git status/history, and build/deployment configuration. Read the actual code before editing it. Do not assume a file is disposable because it looks old or unfamiliar.
C. Establish a baseline. Run the existing relevant tests/build/lint/type checks when feasible before changing behavior. Record failures that already existed. For performance work, choose a reproducible metric and record baseline values under comparable conditions. If no benchmark exists, add a small repeatable benchmark or clearly state that performance cannot yet be measured.
